 C/LNGPAR:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C C/LNGPAR - stream a wide struct argument onto the stack.
C
C Calling convention:
C   M14 = address of the first word to LOAD
C   M12 = -K, VLM testing before it increments, so the body
C         runs K+1 times and M12 finishes at zero
C   ACC = the word to push first
C
C Result:
C   ACC, then [M14] .. [M14+K-1], have been pushed, and
C   [M14+K] is left in the accumulator.
C
C The caller instantiates that two ways for a struct of N
C words.  When the struct is not the first argument the
C accumulator already holds the previous one, so M14 is the
C struct's own address and M12 = -(N-1): the opening XTS is
C the push of that previous argument.  When it is the first
C there is nothing to push ahead of it, so the caller loads
C word 0 itself, passes M14 one past it and M12 = -(N-2).
C Either way words 0..N-2 land in the argument slots and word
C N-1 is left in the accumulator, where an argument of one
C word would have been.
C===========================================================
 LOOP:14,XTS,
      14,UTM,1
      12,VLM,LOOP
      13, UJ,
        ,END,
